const __ORACLE9="THE ORACLE'S LAYER FORM (binding on you in every round). Break every point down into the layers. Write each layer on its own line, beginning with its tag, in this order: [L1] the KJV verse, quoted with its book, chapter and verse; [L2] each Hebrew or Greek word the point turns on, by its Strong's number from the [L2] SHEET, with its meaning as the sheet gives it; [L3] a further verse, quoted with its reference; [L4] the inference, which stands only on two lower layer kinds and the chain from them. This holds for every link, every premise block, every press and every answer to a press. The charge sentence of a premise list is exempt, as PROVEN STRUCTURE says; the witnesses under it carry the layers. When your opponent presses a word of a verse, your answer gives an [L2] for that word and your [L4] names it. Write \"It fits the link\" only inside the [L4], after the layers. Break your opponent's replies down the same way: for each point of your opponent that you answer or charge, name its layers one by one as your opponent wrote them, and test each: its [L1], whether the verse's words say it; its [L2], whether the word and meaning are as the [L2] SHEET gives them; its [L3], whether that verse carries the point; its [L4], whether the inference rests on two of those layers. Say which layer fails and quote the words that show it. Exploit every weakness that this layer-by-layer test of your opponent's replies finds. Charge each point of your opponent that has a failed layer as its own numbered premise in your UNSUPPORTED-L4 PREMISES list, where it is graded: quote your opponent's own words that carry the point, name each failed layer of it, and under it give the layers that show the failure, the verse under PRESSED WITH: and, where the failure is in a word, the [L2] SHEET row for that word. The list keeps its limit of 6 premises: when more than six points fail, list the six that bear most on your opponent's case. State each charge in the positive form, by